### 纠正错误
1. Chinese china → Chinese porcelain；all over the the world 重复 the；China originated from China：主语重复，改用 porcelain；The producing history → and has a production history
2. Ancient chinese → Ancient Chinese；held → mastered；making chinas：porcelain 为不可数名词，不能加 s
3. Chinas with hard material：缺少谓语，应为 Porcelain is hard in texture；smooth face 用词错误，surface（表面）
4. chinas was → porcelain was；exported to abroad：abroad 是副词，去掉 to；Road of Sivils → Silk Road；was like → was liked
5. a integral → an integral；knowledge（知识）改为 wisdom（智慧）；workers（工人）改为 craftsmen（工匠）

### 美化原句
Chinese porcelain is world-famous. Porcelain originated in China and has a production history of thousands of years. Ancient Chinese people mastered superb skills of making 
porcelain. Porcelain is hard in texture, smooth on the surface and rich in varieties. In ancient times, porcelain was exported overseas via the Silk Road and was popular among 
people from all countries. At present, fine porcelain remains an important cultural symbol of China, demonstrating the wisdom of ancient Chinese craftsmen to the world.


